### Domain exception - content not found from JSONPlaceholder provider
# Depends on upstream provider returning 404 for the selected id.

POST {{host}}/api/content
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-version: 1
x-correlation-id: {{$uuid}}

{
  "contentId": 999999999,
  "provider": "JSONPLACEHOLDER"
}

### Domain exception - content not found from DummyJSON provider
# Depends on upstream provider returning 404 for the selected id.

POST {{host}}/api/content
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-version: 1
x-correlation-id: {{$uuid}}

{
  "contentId": 999999999,
  "provider": "DUMMYJSON"
}

### Application exception - provider unavailable
# Covered by ProviderUnavailableException -> 502.
# This requires the configured upstream provider to be unavailable or return a 5xx response.
# The current public API has no deterministic request-only trigger for this case.

POST {{host}}/api/content
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-version: 1
x-correlation-id: {{$uuid}}

{
  "contentId": 1,
  "provider": "JSONPLACEHOLDER"
}

### Business exception
# Covered by BusinessException -> 400.
# The current public API has no use case that throws BusinessException, so there is no deterministic request-only example.

### Application exception - generic
# Covered by ApplicationException -> 400.
# The current public API has no use case that throws generic ApplicationException, so there is no deterministic request-only example.

### Domain exception - generic
# Covered by DomainException -> 400.
# The current public API currently exposes ContentNotFoundException as the concrete domain exception example above.

### Missing request parameter
# Covered by MissingRequestValueException -> 400.
# The current OpenAPI contract has required headers and request body fields, but no required query/path request parameters.

### Unexpected error
# Covered by fallback exception mapping -> 500.
# The current public API has no deterministic request-only trigger without adding a test-only endpoint or forcing an unhandled runtime failure.
